mel: FYI deployed the sampleapp with js-sdk@0.12.2 to Cloudflare Workers and streaming auth headers are disappearing mid-request.
mel: Logs show header built earlier but absent on outgoing fetch to our backend: `Authorization: Bearer undefined` 
mel: minimal repro attached below (striped down).
mel: ```js
// in worker handler
const res = await fetch(BACKEND_URL, {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${makeToken(user)}` },
  body: streamFromSdk(),
});
```
jordan: hmm does `makeToken` use `Buffer.from(...).toString('base64')` anywhere? Workers don't have Buffer.
sam: yep that is a classic. If the token encode path falls back to Buffer it will throw or produce `undefined` and header gets set to `Bearer undefined`. Do we have a stacktrace?
mel: stack is swallowed by fetch, but reproduces locally with wrangler: `TypeError: Buffer is not defined` in `lib/encoding.js` (sdk deps).
arya: short term fix: swap Buffer usage for `globalThis.btoa` / `TextEncoder` paths in edge bundle. Example: ```js
function base64Encode(input) {
  if (typeof Buffer !== 'undefined') return Buffer.from(input).toString('base64');
  if (typeof btoa !== 'undefined') return btoa(input);
  return base64FromUint8Array(new TextEncoder().encode(input));
}
```
jordan: we should avoid runtime branching where possible — better to ship an edge-specific entry point that uses browser APIs and avoids node polyfills. Add an `exports` subpath like `./edge.js`.
sam: +1. Also set package.json `exports` so bundlers pick the right one: ```json
"exports": {
  ".": {
    "import": "./dist/index.mjs",
    "require": "./dist/index.cjs",
    "edge": "./dist/edge.mjs"
  }
}
```
arya: remember TS types: the edge entry shouldn't import Node typings (like `import type { Buffer } from 'buffer'`). TS complains when users have `types` that assume Node. We should ship a `types/edge.d.ts` that uses `globalThis.crypto` and DOM fetch types.
mel: for immediate mitigation, I pushed a small patch in a branch that replaces Buffer for base64 in the auth path and adds a runtime guard. Can we backport it to a patch release?
jordan: run tests against `wrangler dev` and `miniflare` in CI matrix. Our CI bot can add a job: `matrix: [node, worker]`.
ci-bot: added pipeline job request #5678 -> devex/ci: run-miniflare to PR.
devex-bot: Checklist for the SDK fix: [ ] Add edge export entry [ ] Replace Buffer in auth path [ ] Add edge types declaration [ ] Add wrangler/miniflare CI job [ ] Add a tiny runtime detection util and doc note in README
sam: tiny runtime util idea: ```ts
export const isWorker = typeof WebSocket !== 'undefined' && typeof process === 'undefined';
export const b64 = (s: string) => isWorker ? btoa(s) : Buffer.from(s).toString('base64');
```
arya: prefer feature-detect over `process` tests. `globalThis.crypto?.subtle` is a good hint for edge.
mel: Agreed. I'll open the PR with the Buffer->btoa patch + tests in `wrangler dev` and tag you all. Thanks for quick triage :thumbsup:
jordan: also add a short note in the migration doc about `type: "module"` and `exports` so users on Cloudflare know to pick the edge entry.
mel: will do.
